      "versionNonce": 666120156,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1786380773744,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Semantic Reasoners: Engines (like OWL or RDF\nvalidators) that use formal logic to infer consequences\nand catch contradictions.\n\n- Graph Databases: Systems like Neo4j to query\nexplicit, hard-coded relationships (e.g., checking if\nNode: User_A has an edge of Role: Customer).\n\n- Business Logic Rules: Standard programmatic checks\nensuring that states transition correctly (e.g., an\norder must be \"Shipped\" before it can be \"Delivered\").",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Semantic Reasoners: Engines (like OWL or RDF validators) that use formal logic to infer consequences and catch contradictions.\n\n- Graph Databases: Systems like Neo4j to query explicit, hard-coded relationships (e.g., checking if Node: User_A has an edge of Role: Customer).\n\n- Business Logic Rules: Standard programmatic checks ensuring that states transition correctly (e.g., an order must be \"Shipped\" before it can be \"Delivered\").",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
